## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates dynamic programming skills with state expansion, requiring candidates to track whether the cell removal has been used. It tests proper handling of grid boundary conditions and provides opportunities to discuss space optimization strategies and compare memoization versus tabulation approaches.

## Key Concepts
- DP with auxiliary state tracking
- Space optimization using rolling arrays
- Boundary condition handling
- State transition logic

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPathWithOneRemoval(grid) {
  const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
  const dp0 = Array(m).fill().map(() => Array(n).fill(Infinity));
  const dp1 = Array(m).fill().map(() => Array(n).fill(Infinity));

  dp0[0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp1[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
      if (i > 0) {
        dp0[i][j] = Math.min(dp0[i][j], grid[i][j] + dp0[i-1][j]);
        dp1[i][j] = Math.min(dp1[i][j], grid[i][j] + dp1[i-1][j]);
        dp1[i][j] = Math.min(dp1[i][j], dp0[i-1][j]);
      }
      if (j > 0) {
        dp0[i][j] = Math.min(dp0[i][j], grid[i][j] + dp0[i][j-1]);
        dp1[i][j] = Math.min(dp1[i][j], grid[i][j] + dp1[i][j-1]);
        dp1[i][j] = Math.min(dp1[i][j], dp0[i][j-1]);
      }
    }
  }

  return Math.min(dp0[m-1][n-1], dp1[m-1][n-1]);
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity
- Time: O(m × n) - we process each cell once
- Space: O(m × n) - can be optimized to O(n) using rolling arrays since we only need the previous row

## Why This Is Asked

This problem tests advanced dynamic programming: partitioning with a non-trivial segment cost that depends on min and max, requiring careful state design and in-loop maintenance of subproblem results. It also validates producing both memoized and iterative solutions and analyzing time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- DP with partition states
- In-loop maintenance of running min and max
- Top-down memoization vs bottom-up tabulation
- Time complexity: O(D*N^2); Space: O(D*N)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Top-down memoized
function minCost(A, D){
  const N = A.length;
  const memo = Array.from({length:D+1}, ()=> Array(N).fill(null));
  function solve(d, i){
    if (d === 1){
      let mn = Infinity, mx = -Infinity;
      for (let k = 0; k <= i; k++){ mn = Math.min(mn, A[k]); mx = Math.max(mx, A[k]); }
      return mn * mx;
    }
    if (memo[d][i] != null) return memo[d][i];
    let mn = Infinity, mx = -Infinity; let best = Infinity;
    for (let j = i; j >= d-1; j--){
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[j]); mx = Math.max(mx, A[j]);
      best = Math.min(best, solve(d-1, j-1) + mn*mx);
    }
    memo[d][i] = best; return best;
  }
  return solve(D, N-1);
}

// Bottom-up
function minCostBottom(A, D){
  const N = A.length, INF = 1e18;
  const dp = Array.from({length:D+1}, ()=> Array(N).fill(INF));
  // base: d = 1
  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++){
    let mn = A[i], mx = A[i];
    for (let j = i; j >= 0; j--){
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[j]); mx = Math.max(mx, A[j]);
      if (j === 0) dp[1][i] = Math.min(dp[1][i], mn*mx);
    }
  }
  for (let d = 2; d <= D; d++){
    for (let i = d-1; i < N; i++){
      let mn = A[i], mx = A[i];
      for (let j = i; j >= d-1; j--){
        mn = Math.min(mn, A[j]); mx = Math.max(mx, A[j]);
        dp[d][i] = Math.min(dp[d][i], dp[d-1][j-1] + mn*mx);
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[D][N-1];
}
```
